      "text": "If you are an editor in Africa, India, Pakistan, the Middle East, the Philippines, or anywhere overseas working with creators and business owners, this is the skill that will separate you from basic editors.\n\nThey watch a podcast chronologically, hear the interviewer ask a question, hear the guest answer, then cut that exact section into a reel.\n\nThat is not strategy. That is just trimming.\n\nThe best short form editors think like storytellers.\n\nThe hook might be at minute 19. The context might be at minute 2. The payoff might be at minute 34.\n\nYour job is not to keep the timeline in order.\n\nYour job is to find the most interesting idea, rebuild the context around it, and make the viewer feel like they need to keep watching.\n\nViral videos are not built by accident. They are built by studying hooks, patterns, curiosity, pacing, and retention.\n\nIf you are an editor in Africa, India, Pakistan, the Middle East, the Philippines, or anywhere overseas working with creators and business owners, this is the skill that will separate you from basic cutters.\n\nI broke this down in the YouTube video dm me for it or comment \"EDIT\" and I'll send it to you.",
